Revision history for RPi-EEPROM-AT24C32

1.00 UNREL
        - Removed broken, unused eeprom_write_block() XS export (never sent the
          address MSB and read past the end of its 2-byte buffer); single-byte
          writes go through eeprom_write()
        - Added TECHNICAL INFORMATION POD (DEVICE SPECIFICS, MEMORY MAP, ON
          THE WIRE, DATASHEET): chip capabilities, wiring, the 4096-byte/
          128-page layout, and the exact SMBus frames eeprom_read()/
          eeprom_write() put on the bus, verified against the Atmel doc0336
          datasheet
        - Bundled the datasheet as docs/datasheet/AT24C32.pdf and repointed
          the DATASHEET POD section at it instead of the web URL
        - Replaced the fixed post-write sleep with datasheet acknowledge
          polling (doc0336 p.9): write() now re-addresses the chip until it
          ACKs, waiting the real t_WR (<=10ms) instead of a guessed 1ms, so a
          following read/write can't land in a running write cycle. The delay
          param is now a rarely-needed ceiling on that poll (floored at 10ms)
        - Removed the dead internal _writeBlock() helper (it backed the deleted
          eeprom_write_block export and was never called) and the unused
          eeprom_close()/eeprom_read_current_byte() XS exports the OO interface
          never used
        - Added HW-free unit tests (t/10-api_and_validation.t) covering the
          removed XS symbols and the address/byte range validators

0.01    2019-06-28
        - initial version released
        - ability to write/read single bytes

